Original Rawr
-------------
JRawr is a port of Rawr v2.3.23.0, the World of Warcraft (Wrath of the
Lich King 3.3.5a) gear theorycrafting and optimization tool.

Copyright 2008 Chadd Nervig, "HugeHoss", "Toskk", and the Rawr Developers.
Rawr is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

WotLK 3.3.5a fork and port snapshot
-----------------------------------
JRawr was ported from the "RAWR_WotLK_3.3.5a" fork, which updated Rawr to
read item data from a WotLK 3.3.5a database rather than the post-Cataclysm
Wowhead database. The fork was maintained by Magmonix
(https://github.com/Magmonix), with Wine/Mono integration and debugging work
by Adriano Botti.

The read-only port source and the oracle tools used to produce the golden
JSON are archived at
https://github.com/AdrianoBotti/JRawrOriginalRawrSnapshot, tag
`jrawr-oracle-1`. The commit used by the port headers is
46f190bee32964cc8df5fe853d95b8a343f5aa23. The archived snapshot adds the
required WotLK data caches and attribution files; it is otherwise the fork
source.

What JRawr changes
------------------
JRawr is a translation of the original engine to Java 25, not a
line-by-line copy. The deliberate changes are:

  * The calculation engine, all 20 class/spec models, the optimizer and the
    character XML handling are ported to Java and verified with
    golden-master tests against the original compiled binaries.
  * The original WinForms, Silverlight and WPF user interfaces are not
    ported. JRawr has a new Spring Boot web interface using Thymeleaf and
    htmx.
  * Model discovery uses an explicit registry instead of runtime
    reflection.
  * Game data is loaded at runtime from the original XML schemas. The data
    caches are unchanged.
  * The GPL-licensed Cephes special-function code in the original
    `SpecialFunction.cs` was not ported. JRawr uses Apache Commons Math for
    gamma, logGamma, erf, erfc and the regularized beta functions.
  * A companion addon, JRawrCharacterExporter
    (https://github.com/AdrianoBotti/JRawrCharacterExporter), exports the
    active in-game character as Rawr XML.

